@title Harvest 2026 Summary
@subtitle Marlow Valley Extension Service, survey of 214 farms
@author Marlow Valley Extension Service
@date 2026-10-10

Results from our harvest survey of 214 farms across five counties, completed on 2026-10-10. Rainfall tracked yield closely this season: the wettest county led every crop and the driest trailed in every crop.

## Harvest at a glance

kpi Farms surveyed | 214 | completed 2026-10-10

kpi Region rainfall | 601 mm | season average
kpi Wheat | 7.2 t/ha | region average
kpi Corn | 10.0 t/ha | region average
kpi Soybeans | 3.3 t/ha | region average
kpi Barley | 5.9 t/ha | region average

## Yields by county

Yields are in tonnes per hectare; rainfall is season total in millimetres. Calder had the best yield in every crop and Dunmore the lowest.

data harvest = county,rain mm,wheat,corn,soybeans,barley; Calder,701,8.1,11.4,3.7,6.6; Elmstead,655,7.7,10.8,3.5,6.3; Alder,612,7.4,10.2,3.4,6.1; Brennan,548,6.8,9.1,3.1,5.7; Dunmore,489,5.9,8.3,2.8,4.9
data avg = measure,value; Rain mm,601; Wheat,7.2; Corn,10.0; Soybeans,3.3; Barley,5.9

table harvest heat=wheat,corn,soybeans,barley title="Yield by county (t/ha), wettest first"

