table avg title="Region averages"

## Rainfall and yield

The counties line up the same way on rainfall as on yield. Dunmore, the driest at 489 mm, produced 5.9 t/ha of wheat, 2.2 t/ha below Calder, the wettest at 701 mm.

chart hbar harvest y=rain mm unit=mm target="601 region avg" title="Season rainfall by county"

! Rainfall is one factor among many. Soil, planting dates and inputs also differ between counties, so treat this as a strong pattern, not proof of cause.
